  "gloss": "go up, rise; bring up; on, above",
  "summary": "עָלָה is upward movement: people ascend, water or smoke rises, and plants come up. The hiphil brings something up, including an offering presented on the altar; related words name an ascent, a step, an upper room, or what is high. עַל expresses being on or over something and extends to opposition, concern, and cause. Leaves, a pestle, a water-channel and healing remain in the family, without treating their links to rising as settled.",
